# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) to configure a TURN relay.
#
# Without a relay, a room only connects when both networks allow a direct
# peer-to-peer path. Two home networks behind symmetric NAT, or any network
# that blocks UDP, need a relay — see "Connection notes" in README.md.
#
# URLs are comma-separated. Plain `turn:` URLs also get a `?transport=tcp`
# twin automatically, so a UDP-blocked network can still relay.
# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:turn.example.com:3478,turns:turn.example.com:5349
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=photobooth
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=secret
#
# Overrides the STUN server used alongside the relay. Defaults to Google's.
# VITE_STUN_URLS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302
